You have correctly identified two critical issues that drastically affect user experience and data security.
Here is exactly what went wrong and how we are going to fix both:
 1. **The Missing Red Cross (UI Bug):** The frontend was already programmed to show the Red Cross, but it wasn't triggering because the backend wasn't sending the raw BATCH_STATUS to the frontend grid. It evaluated to undefined, so the grid ignored the rejection state.
 2. **Data Visibility (Security Bug):** The backend SQL query was running a generic SELECT * without filtering for the logged-in user.
Here are the precise, professional code changes required for both the Backend and the Frontend to solve these issues.
### Step 1: Update the Backend Service (VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java)
We must update your getAllRequestsSummary method. We will add a userId parameter so it filters by p.CREATED_BY, and we will explicitly map the BATCH_STATUS so the frontend grid knows exactly when to trigger the Red Cross.
*Note: Make sure to also update your interface VoucherRequestService.java to accept the userId parameter: List<Map<String, Object>> getAllRequestsSummary(String userId);*
**Replace your getAllRequestsSummary method with this:**
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getAllRequestsSummary(String userId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                p.BATCH_ID, 
                p.VID_FK,
                p.CREATED_BY AS CREATOR_ID, 
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, p.CREATED_BY) AS CREATOR_NAME,
                p.CREATED_AT AS REQ_DATE, 
                p.RECORDS_COUNT AS TOTAL_ROWS, 
                p.BATCH_STATUS, 
                w.WORKFLOW_STAGE, 
                w.WORKFLOW_CODE,
                w.WORKFLOW_ORDER
            FROM VOUCHER_POSTING p
            LEFT JOIN WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS w ON p.PENDING_AT = w.WORKFLOW_ID
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON p.CREATED_BY = u.USER_ID
            WHERE UPPER(TRIM(p.CREATED_BY)) = UPPER(TRIM(?)) -- SECURITY FIX: Only fetch batches owned by the logged-in user
            ORDER BY p.CREATED_AT DESC
        """;

        return jdbcTemplate.query(sql, (rs, rowNum) -> {
            Map<String, Object> map = new HashMap<>();
            map.put("batchId", rs.getString("BATCH_ID"));
            map.put("vid", rs.getString("VID_FK"));
            map.put("creatorId", rs.getString("CREATOR_ID"));
            map.put("creatorName", rs.getString("CREATOR_NAME"));
            map.put("requestDate", rs.getTimestamp("REQ_DATE"));
            map.put("requestCount", rs.getLong("TOTAL_ROWS"));
            map.put("approvalWorkflow", rs.getString("WORKFLOW_CODE"));
            map.put("workflowState", rs.getString("WORKFLOW_STAGE")); 
            map.put("currentOrder", rs.getObject("WORKFLOW_ORDER")); 
            
            String bStatus = rs.getString("BATCH_STATUS");
            map.put("batchStatus", bStatus); // UI FIX: Explicitly send this flag so the frontend triggers the Red Cross

            if ("R".equals(bStatus)) map.put("currentStatus", "REJECTED");
            else if ("A".equals(bStatus) || "C".equals(bStatus)) map.put("currentStatus", "POSTED");
            else map.put("currentStatus", rs.getString("WORKFLOW_STAGE") != null ? rs.getString("WORKFLOW_STAGE") : "PENDING");

            return map;
        }, userId); // Pass the user ID into the SQL query
    }

```
### Step 2: Update the Backend Controller (VoucherPostingController.java)
Because the Service method now requires a userId, we must extract it from the user's JWT authorization token and pass it down.
**Update your getAllRequestsSummary endpoint mapping in the Controller:**
```java
    @GetMapping("/all-requests-summary")
    public ResponseEntity<?> getAllRequestsSummary(@RequestHeader("Authorization") String token) {
        try {
            // Extract the user ID directly from the active session token
            String userId = jwtTokenUtil.extractUserId(token.substring(7)); 
            
            // Pass it to the service to ensure strictly filtered results
            return ResponseEntity.ok(voucherRequestService.getAllRequestsSummary(userId));
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR)
                    .body(Map.of("status", "Error", "message", "Failed to fetch user requests."));
        }
    }

```
